Z||000000||Mach10||04-22-2001||06:11 PM||||Took a look at the information around on options available to Fiero owners concerning performance upgrades, and decided that things were dispersed a little far. So, at the (sort of) urging of a couple of people on this forum, I've decided to compile information on any performance modification that I can find for the Fiero. This will include engine swaps, turbos, Nitrous, anything. It will take a while, but I have a whole summer available to me, with the GF going away (*sob*) to work.<P>So, if anyone would send the information regarding any modifications done to a Fiero (perf. numbers, costs, problems, parts list if available, approx time to complete, small-size pics) or the links to where I can find this info (WEBMASTERS: I will be in contact w. you for permissions, and credits etc.) it'd be much appreciated. I will do some snooping of my own, and have all sorts of neat stuff on it. Send all the stuff to:<BR>                          umfoggsd&lt;at&gt;mail&lt;dot&gt;cc&lt;dot&gt;umanitoba&lt;dot&gt;ca<BR>Just remove the spam-bot-jammer stuff  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I will post the URL once the page is complete, or has enough to be worth-while.||||reg||7
Z||000001||Spektyr||04-22-2001||06:34 PM||||Awesome idea Mach, wish there was something I could do to help, I'm a Fiero newbie unfortunately.<P>If I may make a suggestion?  A section for cheap/free ways to make your Fiero better.<P>Like removing the screen under the cowl vents (is supposed to improve heat dissapation in the engine compartment) or the lower temp thermostat / fan switch combo to improve stop and go drive-ability.<P>I'll shut up now, and just be happy to see the site.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"><P>------------------<BR>85 GT (to be modified...)<BR>--Um, no the paint isn't oxidized, that's the ultra-rare Whirlpool White textured finish... yeah.<BR>89 Lincoln Town Car (has Fiero Envy)<BR>--Hey!  Can I have an anti-sway bar too?||||reg||1
Z||000002||Mach10||04-22-2001||06:56 PM||||Yup, that's the idea. I kind of want to flex some programming muscle too, and will eventually implement a database style mod suggestion tool, based on desired output, budget, and amount of work. I will be trolling the net like crazy looking for stuff (Nothing copied w/o permission, of course)like this.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Old Lar||04-23-2001||12:13 PM||||The screen on the bottom of the cowl vents is to keep crap from falling into the engine compartment. I don't think taking them off helps with any significant cooling of the engine compartment.<P>Cheap fixes for improved operation don't exist. A tune up, new distributor cap, pickup coil, wires, a good coil are what is needed and that may not be your idea of what is cheap.||||reg||1
